  "term": "phytoestrogen",
  "definition": "A phytoestrogen is a plant-derived compound that can mimic some effects of estrogen by binding to estrogen receptors inside cells and on cell membranes. In the packet, genistein from soybean is described as an isoflavone phytoestrogen.",
